6.How to Secure REST API In java, Especially in springboot,So we use security concepts
Ans) Use Spring Security (Foundation)
we secure REST APIs using Spring Security by implementing authentication and authorization. Commonly, we use JWT for stateless authentication, encrypt passwords using BCrypt, 
and protect endpoints with role-based access control. We also enforce HTTPS and proper CORS configuration

The core security framework for Spring apps is Spring Security.

It helps you:

Authenticate users
Authorize access (roles/permissions)
Protect endpoints
Basic setup:
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain securityFilterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
            .csrf().disable()
            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
                .requestMatchers("/public/**").permitAll()
                .anyRequest().authenticated()
            )
            .httpBasic();

        return http.build();
    }
}
